From 27cb32c5ff156790a8cf19c3aeaf1621e8754040 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Johannes=20Br=C3=BCderl?= <johannes.bruederl@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:41:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(fdbgo): borrow the conflict slab at commit capture, not
 copy it

captureCommit copied every operand and conflict bound into a fresh arena
so a concurrent reset could not rewrite bytes the commit RPC still ships:
23% of allocated bytes on a 50-Set commit. The bytes already live in the
append-only slab (or in buffers nothing rewrites), so the capture now
borrows the slab; reset neither reuses in place nor pools a borrowed slab,
and the commit releases it before publishCommit. Vectors are still copied.
Wire bytes are unchanged.
